nfield and  you know hey look let's throw throw on  out of the back of the end zone if it's  not there but let's let's at least  stress the defense maybe somebody slips  maybe somebody's falls down so I think  in that position you always want to take  a shot I think we've seen Jason Garrett  get taken a task a couple of times  already this year for being too  conservative not going forward on fourth  down earlier this year so I think that's  just his coaching style I think time  management has not been his forte and I  feel like every year we're talking about  at least two or three games where they  could have used their time better but  even even before all that you know  I just I don't understand why is he  killing it is not more of an emphasis  we can a week out because their defense  is playing pretty good yeah and you know  you their offensive line has actually  struggled this year in pass protection  and any offensive line that is  struggling to protect the quarterback  the way you give them confidence the way  you give them some rhythm is just run  the football and they refuse to do it  hey Shawn O'Hara the NFL Network analyst  former Super Bowl champ with the Giants  the Jags are a mess right now certainly  at quarterback Blake bortles getting  benched  Cody Kessler comes in this is a team  that obviously had Super Bowl  aspirations fighting in the locker room  here can you solve this by bringing in  another quarterback Colin Kaepernick may  be trading for Eli Manning is there a  quick fix here for Jacksonville jag no  there's not and really to be on to the  biggest surprise of all is this defense  because they're healthy  you know the offense they've already  gone through two left tackles cam  Robinson blew his knee out against the  Patriots Josh wells are back of left  tackle who came in and played well he  got hurt things are so bad they sign  Derrick flowers of all people and you  think about the injuries that the  running backs they just traded for  Car